FIX FE CD-PLAYER SCREEN (823): reconstruct View_CD_Player @0x451f70 + int-type handlers

Main-screen "CD Player" (main table @0x4697cc screen 4 ACTION 0x451f70) is a 4-category track
controller (Prev.Track / Play / Stop / Next Track; descriptor @0x469ea0 stride 0x14, setup @+4,
action @+8). The main fn + 5 of the 9 category handlers were never decompiled / were void-typed
and unregistered -> raw VAs in the descriptor -> trapped on wasm (same unreconstructed-handler +
int-typing class as View Statistics 821 / Sound Volume 822 / patches 816-818).

Reconstructed 1:1 from objdump of dd2h.exe:
- View_CD_Player @0x451f70: the category loop (LEFT/RIGHT nav via byte tables 0x469eec/0x469eee,
  0x4000 accept, 0x1000 exit; action result != 0 exits). int(void).
- Missing setups 0x4521c4 ("Stop") / 0x4521d8 ("Next Track") + actions 0x45220c (Play ->
  Start_CD_Audio) / 0x452228 (Stop) / 0x452230 (Next Track, track idx @0x469efc cap 0x10)
  reconstructed. Existing void setups 0x45219c/0x4521b0 widened void->int.
- All 9 handlers + the main fn registered so dd2_relocate rewrites the descriptor VAs.

Disproves the "toolchain call_indirect bug" for the last blocked deep screen: unregistered
raw-VA handlers, not a binaryen anomaly.

